course: dictionary
lesson: 4828
title: Hurtful words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hurtful means making someone feel upset or sad, usually because of unkind words or actions. The hurt is in the feelings, not the body. «Hurtful comments» are remarks that make someone feel bad about themselves.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Some words are hurtful or offensive even if the child saying them does not know their meaning.» The sentence tells you that a word can be hurtful even when the person who says it did not mean to be unkind. So hurtful describes what the words do to the person who hears them.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «unkind» in place of «hurtful» in «Saying someone can't be or do something because of their skin colour is wrong and unkind». It still makes sense, so unkind is close in meaning. Hurtful is the word for what unkind words do to someone's feelings.
fact: Hurtful means making someone feel upset or sad, usually because of unkind words or actions.
fact: «Hurtful» is an adjective: hurtful, more hurtful, most hurtful.
fact: «Hurtful comments», «hurtful names» and «hurtful jokes» are all things that can hurt feelings.
fact: Teasing can become hurtful, and if you were hurtful to someone, you should say sorry.
fact: Being anonymous online does not make hurtful words hurt less, because real people read them.
exercise: «Saying someone can't be or do something because of their skin colour is wrong and hurtful.» What does hurtful mean here? | Very loud and noisy | *Making someone feel upset or sad, because of unkind words or actions | Happy and fun to be around | Making someone's skin itch
exercise: The lesson says teasing can become hurtful. What does that mean? | Teasing always makes everyone laugh | Teasing makes the teaser feel tired | Teasing is always kind | *Teasing can make someone feel upset or sad
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to hurtful? | cheerful | quick | quiet | *cruel
test: «Being anonymous online doesn't make hurtful words hurt less; real people read them.» Why do hurtful words still hurt online? | *Real people read them and can be upset | The writer's name is always shown | They only hurt computers | Nobody can ever read words online
test: If you were hurtful to someone, what should you do? | *Say sorry | Say the same thing again to be sure | Laugh about it with your friends | Ignore it and hope they forget
exam: «The Buddhist Udanavarga says: "Hurt not others in ways that you yourself would find hurtful".» What is the lesson of this quote? | Hurt people as often as you can | Only hurt people who were unkind to you first | *Do not treat others in ways you would find hurtful yourself | Hurting others is fine if you are laughing
